# Vulnerability details

### Impact
The `FeeSplitter` contract's `claimFees` function is vulnerable to an exploit where users can steal fees from other token holders. By repeatedly transferring a small amount of subject tokens and calling `claimFees`, a user can claim more fees than entitled to, due to the lack of a mechanism tracking the duration of token holding. This vulnerability could lead to unfair fee distribution and loss of fees for legitimate token holders.

---

### Proof of Concept
In `FeeSplitter.sol`, the `claimFees` function calculates claimable fees based on the current token balance without considering the duration for which the tokens were held. Malicious users can exploit this by transferring tokens back and forth between accounts and claiming fees, effectively "stealing" fees that should have been distributed to longer-term holders.

#### Code Snippet:
```solidity
function claimFees(address token) external {
    // @audit-issue H-03 Vulnerability to fee theft via token transfer
    updateFeeCredit(token, msg.sender);
    uint256 claimable = getClaimableFees(token, msg.sender);
    if (claimable == 0) revert NoFeesToClaim();
    tokensData[token].unclaimedFees[msg.sender] = 0;
    payable(msg.sender).transfer(claimable);
    emit FeesClaimed(token, msg.sender, claimable);
}
```

