# Vulnerability details

## Impact
A griefer can mint rogue tokens into the system by calling ``curves.mint()`` with the malicious contract. This bypasses the ``onlyTokenSubject()`` check. 
This deploys a curveerc20 token, and purchases can start through the buy functions.  
The issue here is the ``_addOwnedCurvesTokenSubject()`` , that is called when a user gets transferred a new token. 
But since a malicious user can keep minting different addresses through ``curves.mint()`` , and buying small amounts, and transferring them using the ``curves.transferCurvesToken()``, they can cause the number of tokens stored in the  ``ownedCurvesTokenSubjects`` for a  user to exceed the gas limit. 

This will cause all new transfers to that address to be reverted due to exceeding the gas limit. 
This is because the all transfers iterate over the ``ownedCurvesTokenSubjects`` for a  user. 
