# Vulnerability details

The batchClaiming function iterates over a list of tokens and updates the fee credit for each one. If the list is too long, the transaction may run out of gas and fail.

```
function batchClaiming(address[] calldata tokenList) external {
        uint256 totalClaimable = 0;
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < tokenList.length; i++) {
            address token = tokenList[i];
            updateFeeCredit(token, msg.sender);
            uint256 claimable = getClaimableFees(token, msg.sender);
            if (claimable > 0) {
                tokensData[token].unclaimedFees[msg.sender] = 0;
                totalClaimable += claimable;
                emit FeesClaimed(token, msg.sender, claimable);
            }
        }
        if (totalClaimable == 0) revert NoFeesToClaim();
        payable(msg.sender).transfer(totalClaimable);
    }

    receive() external payable {}
}

```

### Mitigation

Allow users to specify a subset of their token list to process in a single transaction.
This approach reduces the amount of computation and storage operations in a single transaction, thus reducing the risk of hitting the gas limit.


