# Vulnerability details

The transferAllCurvesTokens function could potentially run out of gas if a user has a large number of token subjects, as it iterates over all owned token subjects to transfer them.

```
function transferAllCurvesTokens(address to) external {
    address[] storage subjects = ownedCurvesTokenSubjects[msg.sender];
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < subjects.length; i++) {
        uint256 amount = curvesTokenBalance[subjects[i]][msg.sender];
        if (amount > 0) {
            _transfer(subjects[i], msg.sender, to, amount);
        }
    }
}
```

### Impact

The gas limit for a block imposes a cap on the amount of computation that can be done in a single transaction. If the transferAllCurvesTokens function tries to transfer an excessive number of tokens, it could exceed the block gas limit, causing the transaction to fail. This could effectively lock a user's ability to transfer all their tokens at once, especially if they have interacted with many different token subjects.

### Mitigation

The contract could implement a paginated transfer function that allows users to specify a range of indices to transfer, thus splitting the transfer over multiple transactions if necessary.



