## Impact
Once `holdersFeePercent` is set via `setExternalFeePercent` function, `onBalanceChange` function will always revert and no user can buy any CurveToken.
Thus, permanently disabling the core functionality of this protocol.

## Bug
The vulnerability stems due to not setting `Curves` contract as `manager` in `FeeSplitter` contract. `FeeSplitter` contract inherits `Security` contract. Only owner who deploys this contract will become the `owner` and `manager` of this contract and can call functions with `onlyManager` modifiers.

As shown in the code below, both the functions have `onlyManager` modifier which restricts access to them.
```javascript
function onBalanceChange(address token, address account) public onlyManager {}
function addFees(address token) public payable onlyManager {}
```
And both of them are called in `_transferFees` function in `Curves` contract as shown in the code below. `Curves` contract is not the `manager` of `FeeSplitter` contract and cannot call these functions.
```javascript
