The `_addOwnedCurvesTokenSubject` function in `Curves.sol` at line 328 becomes progressively more expensive to execute over time. This issue is exacerbated by the absence of a check for zero-amount transfers, allowing malicious actors to inflate the `ownedCurvesTokenSubjects` array by repeatedly transferring zero tokens. This can lead to prohibitively high gas costs for functions interacting with this array, potentially rendering them unusable or susceptible to Denial of Service (DoS) attacks.

---

