# Vulnerability details

## Description
Token holders can earn rewards when `holdersFeePercent` is specified in the `feeEconomics` state variable. These rewards are distributed proportionally among all holders.

The FeeSplitter contract uses the `TokenData` struct to record the reward details of each  token holder. 

    struct TokenData {
        uint256 cumulativeFeePerToken;
        mapping(address => uint256) userFeeOffset;
        mapping(address => uint256) unclaimedFees;
    }

The `cumulativeFeePerToken` stores how much reward each internal Curve token has earned. The `userFeeOffset` mapping stores the value of  `cumulativeFeePerToken` at the last time a user balance changed. The `unclaimedFees` mapping saves the amount each user has earned but not claimed.

When a user's balance changes, the reward he has earned is calculated as `(cumulativeFeePerToken - userFeeOffset) * balanceOf(token, user)`. The reward is added to his `unclaimedFees` and his `userFeeOffset` is updated to the current value of `cumulativeFeePerToken`.

This is done in the `updateFeeCredit` function:
```solidity
    function updateFeeCredit(address token, address account) internal {
        TokenData storage data = tokensData[token];
        uint256 balance = balanceOf(token, account);
        if (balance > 0) {
            uint256 owed = (data.cumulativeFeePerToken - data.userFeeOffset[account]) * balance;
            data.unclaimedFees[account] += owed / PRECISION;
            data.userFeeOffset[account] = data.cumulativeFeePerToken;
        }
    }
```

