## Vulnerability Details
`FeeSplitter::claimFees` function calls [getClaimableFees](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/main/contracts/FeeSplitter.sol#L73-L78) to fetch claimable rewards of an account. account rewards are [calculated by multiplying `data.userFeeOffset[account]` in `data.cumulativeFeePerToken`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/main/contracts/FeeSplitter.sol#L76) (accumulated rewards) and then [adding them to unclaimed rewards of account](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/main/contracts/FeeSplitter.sol#L77). 
To prevent a single account from claiming excessive rewards, [`data.userFeeOffset[account]` is updated to `data.cumulativeFeePerToken`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/main/contracts/FeeSplitter.sol#L69). this means that to be able to claim excessive rewards we must find a way to reset `data.userFeeOffset[account]` to `0` and have balance > 0. which is [completely possible by transferring curves to another account](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/main/contracts/Curves.sol#L313-L325), the reason is that `data.userFeeOffset[to]` is not updated upon receiving new tokens.

