# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The `subjects` array in `_addOwnedCurvesTokenSubject` can grow infinitely and is used in a `for` loop block that can exceed the block gas limit. This particular instance was not caught and is not included in the bot report.

## Proof of Concept

The `_addOwnedCurvesTokenSubject` is called every time a user receives tokens from a `curvesTokenSubject` for the first time. Thus, the `curvesTokenSubject` address is pushed to `subjects` array.

```solidity
    function _addOwnedCurvesTokenSubject(address owner_, address curvesTokenSubject) internal { 
        address[] storage subjects = ownedCurvesTokenSubjects[owner_]; 
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < subjects.length; i++) { //@audit this can run out of gas - not in the bot report
            if (subjects[i] == curvesTokenSubject) {
                return;
            }
        }
        subjects.push(curvesTokenSubject);
    }
```

However, there is no `pop` method even if the user sells the tokens from a specific `curvesTokenSubject` and doesn't hold tokens anymore. This will lead to the `subjects` array growing too big, reverting with Out-Of-Gas error, and causing DoS.

## Tools Used

Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Consider removing the `curvesTokenSubject` from the array when the user sells his tokens or capping the size of the array to a fixed number.


## Assessed type

DoS

