## Impact
Any user has the ability to set arbitrary `curves` in `FeeSplitter`. 
Consequently, a malicious user can revert the fee splitting by setting malicious `curves`.
## Proof of Concept
1. A malicious user can set non-contract accounts or contracts that return 0 for the `curvesTokenSupply` and `curvesTokenBalance` functions as `curves`.
```
function setCurves(Curves curves_) public {
    curves = curves_;
}
