Both buy and sell call `_transferFees`, so the token owner can make the token unpurchasable or unsellable.

Since the price of the token is calculated according to the supply, the token owner has reason to prevent the user from selling the token and keep the token price high.

The token owner can judge whether users buy or sell tokens through the algorithm in fallback, such as judging by the reduction or increase of supply. The token owner can also deploy updatable contract accounts for manipulation.

`referral` is set up by the token owner, but it may also be for the purpose of a DoS attack, preventing users from buying or selling tokens.

