> This issue is related to [L-12](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/main/bot-report.md#l-12-unbounded-loop-may-run-out-of-gas) submitted by the bot. I’m submitting it as a Medium to emphasize the importance of fixing it, to safeguard users from spending unnecesarily large amounts of ETH when buying or transferring tokens.
> 

## Implementation Details

The `ownedCurvesTokenSubjects` mapping is used to track which tokens a user holds:

```solidity
mapping(address => address[]) private ownedCurvesTokenSubjects;
```

When buying or transferring tokens, the `_addOwnedCurvesTokenSubject` function is called, to update the array of token addresses:

```solidity
// Internal function to add a curvesTokenSubject to the list if not already present
function _addOwnedCurvesTokenSubject(address owner_, address curvesTokenSubject) internal {
    address[] storage subjects = ownedCurvesTokenSubjects[owner_];
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < subjects.length; i++) {
        if (subjects[i] == curvesTokenSubject) {
            return;
        }
    }
    subjects.push(curvesTokenSubject);
}
```

This function’s time complexity is O(n), with `n` being the amount of owned token subjects.

> Also note that the `for` loop is not well optimized, so it consumes a lot of gas.
> 

