## Impact
Due to flawed logic in the way that claimable fees are calculated, a malicious user can claim fees an infinite number of times (until FeeSplitter.sol) is drained.

## Proof of Concept
When there is a holder's fee set in the protocol, whenever a user buys a token, a percentage of the fees (holder's fee) is sent to the FeeSplitter.sol in order later to be re-distributed to the users as an incentive for holding the tokens in the Curves ecosystem.

The logic in which the claimable fees are calculated is inherently flawed allowing for a malicious user to claim fees multiple times until the contract's funds are drained.

The function `claimFees()`: 

