# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The identified vulnerability in the feeSplitter contract significantly impacts the fairness and security of the ETH fees distribution system. The claimableFees mechanism favors early holders because the amount of claimable fee depends not only on the user's current token balance but also on the timing of their purchase.

A critical consequence of this design is that it incentivizes hodling of the token. A malicious actor, aware of this flaw, can manipulate the system to their advantage. By purchasing tokens late with a different wallet and then transferring these tokens to their early-buyer wallet, they can artificially inflate their claimable amount of ETH by using the early-buyer wallet.

This attack can lead to claimable amounts sum higher than feeSplitter contract balance and thus draining the contract balance and some late claimers won't be able to receive their promised returns

The broader implications include a loss of trust in the system, and a negative impact on the token's market perception


