# Vulnerability details

## Summary

The mapping `ownedCurvesTokenSubjects` is an array storing a list of every single Curve tokens owned by an address. However, the function `_addOwnedCurvesTokenSubject()` loops through said entire array once every call. Said function is called on every token transfers.

We show that, through normal usage, the array size will be inflated, becoming prohibitively gas-expensive for the user to receive new tokens or buying new tokens, to the point of DOS by out-of-gas.

We also show an attack vector, where any user can grief any other user by creating such a DoS scenario (or to simply inflate gas cost to transfer tokens to them, eventually also up to a DoS), without even having to buy any Curves tokens. 

We also show that, using that exact attack, anyone can brick functions `deposit()`, and even without that, it will also brick itself through normal usage.

