# Vulnerability details

The _transferFees() function utilizes a push-over-pull method of transferring ether. A curvesSubject is the one who buys the first curves token and his address is the index for all the curve token logic. The curvesSubject denies his subjects(followers who own curves tokens) to sell the curvesSubject tokens. 

The issue comes from allowing the curvesSubject to set the referral address. Which can be a contract that always reverts transactions.

There are 2 scenarios that curvesSubject can perform:
1) Grief the protocol by forcing his followers to hold the tokens.
2) curvesSubject can buy lots of his tokens in the second round, then his subjects start to buy more of the tokens. Whenever his subjects want to sell tokens, he will front-run to "lock" the protocol and then "unlock" it. Whenever a follower wants to buy, he will not "lock" it, thus boosting his curvesSubject. At the peak of the price, he then dumps all of it.

## Impact
1) Users are not able to sell their tokens and ether stuck in the contract.
2) curvesSubject can manipulate the price to his favor as per 2nd scenario.


