# Vulnerability details

In `Security.sol`, there are two modifiers, `onlyOwner` and `onlyManager`, designed to verify whether the msg.sender is authorised. 

However, these modifiers lack "require" statements to enforce the condition that the returned boolean must be true. 

As a result, anyone can call functions that are intended to be restricted.

## Impact

Due to the absence of "require" statements, restricted functions can be executed without proper verification of the boolean return values. Consequently, unauthorized users gain access to admin functions and can modify configurations, potentially causing severe disruptions to the protocol.

## Proof of Concept

[Security.sol#L8-L16](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-01-curves/blob/516aedb7b9a8d341d0d2666c23780d2bd8a9a600/contracts/Security.sol#L8-L16)

```solidity
    modifier onlyOwner() {
        msg.sender == owner;
        _;
    }

    modifier onlyManager() {
        managers[msg.sender] == true;
        _;
    }
```


